[4] Boundary-gap packet theorem readout
  Exact lemma now available for any finite row S:
    S is LRC14-safe with strict slack iff at least one boundary bridge
    between adjacent danger arcs has positive rational length.
  Therefore a strict counterexample in the covering branch must satisfy:
    qdiv(S)>14 and every labelled boundary bridge is pinched to length 0
    after merging danger arcs.
  Audited conclusion:
    zero-open qdiv>14 packets in this bank = 0.
    zero net first-current packets in this bank = 1187.
    Thus the bridge cannot be a raw divergence proof; the useful token is
    the localized transition packet / second moment of the boundary gaps.
  Proof target promoted from a search condition:
    show the localized endpoint-owner transition packet of any qdiv>14
    zero-open row either has positive gK8/L_y moment image or carries a
    K33/H=7 state-lift label.
  This is the boundary-moment bridge in packet form.

[5] Tournament Analysis
  vertices are proof coordinates, not runners.
  pair observable:
    which coordinate preserves the covering LRC predicate and prevents a
    positive boundary gap from being scalarized away.
  switch/gauge:
    lexicographic retention of q-covering, exact gap, endpoint owner,
    source identity, state-lift visibility, moment image, and anti-scalar guard.
  tie Hamiltonian path:
    source_spectrum_pullback > exact_boundary_gap > endpoint_owner_current > gK8_Ly_moment_image > K33_state_lift_packet > C27_unital_packet > fixed_margin_swap_fiber > q_cover_gate > raw_runner_row
